From: Project Luma <luma@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: add FP6 IMX896 C-PHY receive mode

The Fairphone 6 rear-main Sony IMX896 is connected to CSIPHY0 using three
C-PHY trios at 990 Msymbol/s.  Program the Qualcomm CSIPHY 2.2.1 three-phase
mission-mode table and select C-PHY in CSID340 for that fixed board route.

Qualcomm's lane-enable field interleaves D-PHY and C-PHY selections.  The
three C-PHY trios are bits 1, 3, and 5 (0x2a), not the contiguous value 0x07.
Using 0x07 leaves only trio 0 active, overflows CSID lane 0, and produces no
packets.  The 0x2a setting is physically verified on FP6 with a complete
4096x3072 packed RAW10 capture from the IMX896.

This is deliberately limited to SM7635 CSIPHY0, which is the fixed IMX896
route in the FP6 device tree.  Other SM7635 PHYs retain their D-PHY path.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c   |   3 +
 .../platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c      | 124 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 127 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
index 2b50f9b96..3fe7f5982 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
@@ -63,6 +63,9 @@ static void __csid_configure_rx(struct csid_device *csid, struct csid_phy_config
 	val |= FIELD_PREP(CSI2_RX_CFG0_DLX_INPUT_SEL_MASK, phy->lane_assign);
 	val |= FIELD_PREP(CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_MASK,
 			  phy->csiphy_id + CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_BASE_IDX);
+	/* FP6 rear-main on CSIPHY0 uses three-trio C-PHY. */
+	if (phy->csiphy_id == 0)
+		val |= CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_TYPE_SEL;
 	writel_relaxed(val, csid->base + CSID_CSI2_RX_CFG0);
 
 	val = CSI2_RX_CFG1_PACKET_ECC_CORRECTION_EN;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
